        <div id="testing" class="scroll-mt-24">
          <h2 class="text-3xl font-black text-gray-900 mt-16 mb-6">
            8. Testing: NSF Contents Certified Is Not Certified for Sport
          </h2>

          <p>
            Retailer listings for C4 Whey reproduce a packaging claim of NSF Contents Certified. That is a real NSF program, and it is better than nothing: it checks that the label's ingredient and nutrient claims match what is in the tub and screens for certain contaminants. It is a reasonable reassurance that you are getting 25 g of protein and not a protein-spiked filler.
          </p>

          <p>
            It is not the same as NSF Certified for Sport, which adds screening for substances banned by major sports organizations, lot-by-lot testing and facility audits. Several other C4 products, including C4 Sport pre-workout and C4 Performance Energy, are marketed as NSF Certified for Sport. We could not find C4 Whey Protein listed under Certified for Sport or Informed Choice at the time of writing. Cellucor markets a separate product, Whey Sport, to professional athletes under its NSF program.
          </p>

          <p>
            If you compete in a drug-tested sport, that distinction is the whole story. Choose a whey that appears in the NSF Certified for Sport or Informed Choice databases for the exact flavor you buy, and keep the lot number. Our <a href="/best-nsf-certified-protein-powder/">best NSF certified protein powder</a> guide lists options, and Optimum Nutrition and Dymatize, the two alternatives above, both promote Informed Choice certification.
          </p>

          <p>
            On heavy metals, we could not find published test results for C4 Whey from Clean Label Project, Labdoor or Consumer Reports at the time of writing. Whey generally tests low for heavy metals compared with plant proteins, although chocolate flavors tend to carry more because cocoa naturally contains some lead and cadmium. If that concerns you, ask Nutrabolt for its latest test data or choose a vanilla flavor.
          </p>
        </div>

